      <!-- SECTION 6: TESTING CONDITIONS & DISPLAY CALIBRATION -->
      <article class="space-y-6">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3.5 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-900 text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm uppercase font-semibold">
          Standardized Examination Protocols
        </div>
        <h2 class="font-heading font-extrabold text-2xl sm:text-4xl text-zinc-950 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          Testing Conditions & Display Calibration
        </h2>
        <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
          When taking an online color blind test, monitor hardware and ambient lighting introduce environmental variables that must be controlled to prevent false-positive or false-negative results:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 pt-2">
          <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-3xl bg-zinc-50 dark:bg-zinc-900/60 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 space-y-2">
            <div class="mb-2 text-amber-500"><svg class="w-7 h-7" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="5" /><line x1="12" y1="1" x2="12" y2="3" /><line x1="12" y1="21" x2="12" y2="23" /><line x1="4.22" y1="4.22" x2="5.64" y2="5.64" /><line x1="18.36" y1="18.36" x2="19.78" y2="19.78" /><line x1="1" y1="12" x2="3" y2="12" /><line x1="21" y1="12" x2="23" y2="12" /><line x1="4.22" y1="19.78" x2="5.64" y2="18.36" /><line x1="18.36" y1="5.64" x2="19.78" y2="4.22" /></svg></div>
            <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-xl text-zinc-950 dark:text-white">1. Screen Brightness</h3>
            <p class="text-base text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
              Set display brightness between 80% and 100%. Dim backlights diminish chromatic luminance contrast, making vanishing plates artificially difficult to read for trichromatic eyes.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-3xl bg-zinc-50 dark:bg-zinc-900/60 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 space-y-2">
            <div class="mb-2 text-rose-500"><svg class="w-7 h-7" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" /><line x1="4.93" y1="4.93" x2="19.07" y2="19.07" /></svg></div>
            <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-xl text-zinc-950 dark:text-white">2. Disable Blue-Light Filters</h3>
            <p class="text-base text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
              Disable Night Shift, Apple TrueTone, f.lux, or Android Night Light. Blue-light cut software shifts the display color temperature to warm amber, distorting clinical dot matrices.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-3xl bg-zinc-50 dark:bg-zinc-900/60 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 space-y-2">
            <div class="mb-2 text-blue-500"><svg class="w-7 h-7" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M21.3 15.3a2.4 2.4 0 0 1 0 3.4l-2.6 2.6a2.4 2.4 0 0 1-3.4 0L2.7 8.7a2.4 2.4 0 0 1 0-3.4l2.6-2.6a2.4 2.4 0 0 1 3.4 0Z" /><path d="m14.5 12.5 2-2" /><path d="m11.5 9.5 2-2" /><path d="m8.5 6.5 2-2" /><path d="m17.5 15.5 2-2" /></svg></div>
            <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-xl text-zinc-950 dark:text-white">3. Viewing Distance</h3>
            <p class="text-base text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
              Position yourself 50 to 75 cm (~20 to 30 inches) from your monitor at eye level. Avoid direct glare or harsh incandescent reflections on your screen glass.
            </p>
